{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Some problems are not about numbers in a list but about **ranges on a line** — meetings on a calendar, bookings in a hotel, segments on a road. The questions sound different from anything so far: which ranges overlap, how many are active at once, where are the gaps."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The line sweep pattern answers all of them with the same move: **sort, then walk left to right once**, carrying a little state."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The core idea"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Imagine a vertical line sweeping across the timeline from left to right. Nothing interesting happens while it travels through empty space — the state only changes at the moments a range **starts** or **ends**."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "So we do not simulate time continuously. We jump from event to event, in order, updating state as we go."
    },
